\description{
Reads the stable time-series surfaces in the official Budget Economic and
Fiscal Update (BEFU), Half Year Economic and Fiscal Update (HYEFU), and
Pre-election Economic and Fiscal Update (PREFU) chart-data workbooks. This
reader is deliberately limited to the named fiscal, economic, and
key-indicator time-series surfaces; it does not attempt to extract every
table, figure, narrative, or supplementary workbook tab.
}
\details{
Forecast values retain both their publication vintage and the source status
label. Generic \verb{\% of GDP} rows inherit their parent metric when constructing
\code{series}, so a level and its percentage-of-GDP counterpart remain distinct
series identities. Unit context is read from the source labels and is
retained alongside the numeric value. Supported units are \code{"NZD billion"},
\code{"NZD million"}, \code{"percentage points"}, \code{"percent"}, and \code{"index"}.

A local XLSX workbook or canonical CSV can be supplied for an offline,
reproducible replay. Local artifacts are signature-checked, copied to a
hash-addressed raw cache, and parsed through the same validation path as a
downloaded artifact; supplying \code{file} never performs network I/O. Without
a local file, retrieval is HTTPS-only from the official Treasury host and
requires \code{accept_terms = TRUE} after reviewing \code{\link[=nz_fiscal_terms]{nz_fiscal_terms()}}.

The catalogue currently supports the exact EFU release identifiers
\code{"befu-2026"}, \code{"hyefu-2025"}, and \code{"prefu-2023"}. Use
\code{\link[=list_nz_fiscal_releases]{list_nz_fiscal_releases()}} with \code{family = "efu"} to inspect release
status, dates, forecast metadata, official URLs, and expected hashes. With
\code{release_id = NULL}, \code{revision = "as_published"} selects the newest current
catalogue row and falls back to the newest issue date when the family has no
current row; \code{revision = "latest"} always selects the newest issue date. An
explicit \code{release_id} always selects that release; the selected revision
policy is recorded in provenance.

\code{dataset} routes to the following workbook sheets: \code{"fiscal"} to
\code{"Fiscal Time Series"}, \code{"economic"} to \code{"Economic Time Series"}, and
\code{"key_indicators"} to \code{"Table 1"} for BEFU and HYEFU. PREFU uses its
distinct \code{"Executive Summary Table"} sheet for \code{"key_indicators"}. One or
more routes may be requested. XLSX rows are emitted in the requested
dataset order and then in source-sheet order; canonical CSV input retains
its input row order after filtering. The function does not sort
observations.

Each EFU observation represents a June fiscal year: \code{period_end} is June 30
of \code{year} and \code{fiscal_year_basis} is \code{"June year"}. The parser maps source
status labels containing \code{actual} or \code{unaudited} to \code{actual}, and labels
containing \code{forecast} or \code{estimate} to \code{forecast}.
The original \code{source_status_label} remains unchanged. Values remain in the
source scale; \code{unit_multiplier} records the corresponding numeric multiplier
(\code{1e9} for \code{"NZD billion"}, \code{1e6} for \code{"NZD million"}, and \code{1} for the
other supported units). No interpolation, currency conversion, or forecast
revision is performed.

Parsed results use an in-memory parsed-result cache keyed by the raw
SHA-256, release, revision policy, parser version, schema version, and
parser options. Raw snapshots are written below \code{cache_dir}, whose default
is \code{.nz_cache_dir()}, normally
\code{tools::R_user_dir("readfiscalnz", "cache")/v1}; package cache limits are
controlled by the \verb{readfiscalnz.*} options. Reading a local file can create
files below \code{cache_dir} and update cache timestamps, but does not modify the
input artifact. Live retrieval is opt-in, never occurs on package load, and
is HTTPS-only, size-bounded, signature-checked, SHA-256-checked, and
retried only within the package's bounded transport policy.

The parser fails closed when a release, route, local artifact, workbook
identity, required sheet, year/status label, unit context, canonical column
set, or release metadata does not match the supported contract. Common
errors include an unknown \code{release_id}, an \code{update} value inconsistent with
the selected release, an unsupported \code{dataset}, a missing or malformed local
file, a terms refusal for live retrieval, and official transport, size, or
hash failures. No fallback workbook or guessed unit is substituted.
}
